## Relationship: GENUINE INCOMPLETE FIX (confirmed via NVD + Moby GHSA)
  CVE-2024-41110 (GHSA-v23v-6jw2-98fq): AuthZ plugin bypass — a request the plugin is shown
    WITHOUT its body (Content-Length:0 / chunked) is default-allowed while the daemon acts on
    the full body. Fix (commit fc274cd2, v23.0.15/26.1.5/27.1.1) added the || isChunked(r) branch.
  CVE-2026-34040 (GHSA-x744-4wpc-v9h2): INCOMPLETE FIX of -41110 — the same AuthZRequest predicate
    still gates on r.ContentLength < maxBodySize (1 MiB) and drainBody Peek(maxBodySize) returns a
    NIL body for oversized payloads, so a body >= 1 MiB is never shown to the plugin. Fix (commit
    e89edb19, v29.3.1) Peek(maxBodySize+1) and FAIL-CLOSED rejects oversized bodies. SAME sink,
    same file (pkg/authorization/authz.go), same fix lineage. No intervening non-CVE release.

